+# Relay operations
+
+## Startup
+
+From the repository root, start Relay with the command declared in
+`service/relay/service.json`:
+
+```sh
+python3 service/relay/server.py --port 8765
+```
+
+The process binds to `127.0.0.1`, so it is reachable only on the local host. A
+local start with Python 3.13.5 was observed on 2026-09-14.
+
+## Health
+
+Probe the manifest's loopback health endpoint:
+
+```sh
+curl --fail --silent --show-error http://127.0.0.1:8765/health
+```
+
+A local probe on 2026-09-14 returned HTTP 200 and
+`{"status": "ok", "deliveries": 0}`. This establishes local process health only;
+production health and external connectivity were not observed.
+
+## Recovery
+
+For a failed rollout, stop the new process and restart the last reviewed
+revision with the startup command above. A local stop and restart followed by a
+successful health probe was observed on 2026-09-14. Production rollback and
+deployment permissions remain unverified because they are unavailable from a
+local checkout.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+The delivery counter is held in process memory and is lost on restart. The
+service exposes only a loopback listener in this checkout. Production deployment
+access, production health, and production rollback were not tested.
